e W=9 7×7 sub-matrix has det = 1 by row cofactor expansion but no row+col upper-triangulation; ~250 Lean lines per such corner). **Adds EDGE (negative shape, in EDGES.md as a refinement of E2.1)**: leading-row + dead-col triangulation closes E2.1 orthogonal corner exactly for `W ∈ {2, 3, 4, 5, 6, 8, 10, 12, 18, 20}` at `R ≤ 22`. **Cross-domain ingredient**: bitmask DP over reachability (algorithmic, not number-theoretic). **Channelled mathematician**: none — purely combinatorial enumeration. Cites E2.1, references S98/S99/S106/S107/S117/S122/S128/S129/S137/S143/S144 (the closure chain). See `experiments/formalisations/E2_1_mps_bond_dim/leading_row_search.py` and `experiments/formalisations/E2_1_mps_bond_dim/leading_row_search_results.txt`, `archive/sessions/session144_l1_lean_w10_corner_and_search.md`. | 144 |
